  "id": "COMPOUND:32188 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a mechanistic link between 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and the CD276 antigen, mediated through dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This pathway is consistently identified as a target of 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine in multiple paths, with each subsequent entity in the chain—Javanicoside F and Ascidiathiazone B—also targeting CD276. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mode of action remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets in the same pathway suggests a potential role in signaling or cellular regulation, which could be relevant in the context of CD276-related diseases. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine may modulate CD276 through a kinase-dependent mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific interactions and biological relevance.",
